gnancy on the anterior surface of the uterus</article-title><source>Br J Clin Pract</source><year>1978</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>205</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">678418</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref8"><label>8</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kellet</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary abdominal (peritoneal) pregnancy</article-title><source>J Obstet Gynaecol Br Commonw</source><year>1973</year><volume>80</volume><fpage>1102</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4761385</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref9"><label>9</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goh</surname><given-names>TH</given-names></name><name><surname>Rahman</surname><given-names>SA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary peritoneal pregnancy implanted on the uterine fundus</article-title><source>Aust N Z J Obstet Gynecol</source><year>1980</year><volume>20</volume><fpage>240</fpage><lpage>1</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref10"><label>10</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>AG</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary peritoneal pregnancy</article-title><source>Br Med J</source><year>1968</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>96</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5696553</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref11"><label>11</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hatada</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The pedunculated type of primary peritoneal pregnancy implanted on the infundibulopelvic ligament</article-title><source>Obstet Gynecol</source><year>1993</year><volume>82</volume><issue>2 Suppl</issue><fpage>693</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8378016</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref12"><label>12</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Copper</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Early primary peritoneal pregnancy</article-title><source>J Obstet Gynaecol Br Commonw</source><year>1968</year><volume>75</volume><fpage>232</fpage><lpage>3</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5641022</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref13"><label>13</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Friederich</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Primary omental pregnancy.2 cases of primary peritoneal pregnancy</article-title><source>Obstet Gynecol</source><year>1968</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>104</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">5635834</pub-id></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref14"><label>14</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Yackel</surname><given-names>DB</given-names></name><name><surname>Panton</surname><given-names>ON</given-names></name><name><surname>Martin</surname><given-names>DJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Splenic pregnancy: Case report</article-title><source>Obstet Gynaecol</source><year>1988</year><volume>71</volume><fpage>471</fpage><lpage>73</lpage></element-citation></ref><ref id="ref15"><label>15</label><element-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kahn</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Skjeldestad</surname><given-names>FE</given-names></name><name><surname>v During</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Sunde</surname><given-names>A</given-nam